cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "Open Profiling Dataset"
abstract: >-
  A structured, source-traceable dataset of adjudicated serial homicide cases,
  built for criminological and computational research. Every substantive claim
  carries its own citation and its own confidence level; a field either has an
  admissible source or a null value and a note recording what was searched.
  A validator enforces the rule, and the human-readable reports are compiled
  from the structured data rather than written alongside it. The project began
  as an audit of a 200-subject list assembled with a language model, of which
  roughly 20 per cent proved defective, and the sourcing discipline is the
  response to that finding. Code is MIT licensed; data is CC BY-SA 4.0.
type: dataset
authors:
